WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.952
Algorithmic bias, like human 
bias, results in&nbsp;unfairness.

00:00:03.952 --> 00:00:06.805
However, algorithms, like viruses,

00:00:06.805 --> 00:00:09.872
can spread bias on a massive scale

00:00:09.872 --> 00:00:11.395
at a&nbsp;rapid pace.

00:00:11.395 --> 00:00:15.344
Algorithmic bias can also lead 
to exclusionary experiences

00:00:15.344 --> 00:00:17.451
and discriminatory&nbsp;practices.

00:00:17.451 --> 00:00:18.744
So what can we do about it?

00:00:18.744 --> 00:00:22.375
Well, we can start thinking about 
how we create&nbsp;more inclusive code

00:00:22.375 --> 00:00:25.423
and employ inclusive coding practices.

00:00:25.423 --> 00:00:27.698
It really starts with people.

00:00:27.698 --> 00:00:29.532
So&nbsp;who codes matters.

00:00:29.532 --> 00:00:33.698
Are we creating full-spectrum teams 
with diverse individuals

00:00:33.698 --> 00:00:35.862
who can check&nbsp;each other's blind spots?

00:00:35.862 --> 00:00:37.302
How we code matters.

00:00:37.302 --> 00:00:40.543
Are we factoring in fairness as 
we're developing&nbsp;systems?

00:00:40.543 --> 00:00:43.099
And finally, why we code matters.

00:00:43.099 --> 00:00:45.875
We've used tools of computational creation

00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:48.041
to unlock&nbsp;immense wealth.

00:00:48.041 --> 00:00:52.454
We now have the opportunity to 
unlock even greater equality

00:00:52.454 --> 00:00:55.547
if we make social&nbsp;change a priority

00:00:55.547 --> 00:00:57.640
and not an afterthought.

